<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liberal Party (UK)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1859–1988</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Liberal Party was one of the two major parties of the United Kingdom from its formation in 1859, out of the Whigs, Radicals and Peelites, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. Under William Gladstone and later H. H. Asquith and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Lloyd George it championed free trade, Irish Home Rule, a wider franchise and social reform. Overtaken by the Labour Party after 1918, it merged into the Liberal Democrats in 1988.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liberal-party-uk.jpg" alt="Liberal Party (UK)" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dn9ahx (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liberal_Party_logo_(pre1988).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
